    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d992">

                <pb facs="1241" n="1231" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.93/12–1347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-13T17:00:00+08:00">December 13,
                            1947—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 13—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2393. In conversation with me, Foreign Minister has expressed deep concern with
                    regard current rumors here that proposal for $60,000,000 interim aid China has
                    been thrown out in conference possibly at instance State Department. Foreign
                    Minister greatly fears adverse effect internal economic financial situation and
                    if there is basis in fact for these rumors, I am impelled to suggest that a
                    statement from you to general effect that there is no change in our <pb
                        facs="1242" n="1232" xml:id="pg1232"/> over-all policy of desiring
                    adequately to aid China would have reassuring effect at this time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
